         ORDER SETTING STATUS CONFERENCE AND MOTION DEADLINES

         THIS MATTER comes before the Hearing Examiners upon their issuance of the Order

Granting Joint Motion for a Revised Procedural Schedule. The Hearing Examiners, being duly

informed, FIND AND CONCLUDE:

         1.    On November 20, 2025, Southwestern Public Service Company (SPS) filed its

application requesting Commission authorization to revise its retail rates under Advice Notice No.

341.

         2.    On December 15, 2025, the Hearing Examiners issued the Procedural Order, which

established the procedural dates for this docket.

         3.     On March 13, 2026, the Hearing Examiners issued their Order Granting Joint

Motion for a Revised Procedural Schedule, which established a revised procedural schedule and

found that the Hearing Examiners would coordinate a status conference on or before March 31,

2026.

         4.    The Order Granting Joint Motion for a Revised Procedural Schedule established

the following deadlines:

               a. March 20, 2026 – SPS List of Revisions (17.1.3.19(C) NMAC)
                   BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Setting Status Conference and Motion Deadlines          Docket No. 25-00079-UT


               b. May 1, 2026 – Staff and Intervenor Direct Testimony

               c. May 29, 2026 – Rebuttal Testimony

               d. July 7, 2026, at 9am MT – Evidentiary Hearing Begins

       5.      In consideration of the revised procedural schedule, deadlines should be set for

motions in limine, motions to strike testimony, and other prehearing motions.

IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

       A.      A status conference will be held beginning at 11:00 am on Monday, March 30,

2026. The status conference will be held via the Zoom platform. An invitation to the Zoom

videoconference shall be sent by separate e-mail to all persons on the service list. The status

conference is for procedural purposes only; the merits of any part of the case will not be discussed.

Finally, the status conference is reserved only for parties to this matter; the Zoom link shall not be

shared with anyone who is not a recognized party to this case.

       B.      Any motions in limine, motions to strike testimony, and other prehearing motions

shall be filed on or before June 12, 2026. Responses to such motions shall be filed on or before

June 23, 2026.

       ISSUED under the Seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, this 20th day of

March, 2026.

                                NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION



                                 Keven Gedko
                                 Co-Hearing Examiner



                                 Patrick Schaefer
